OL,3,GNEWSAHigh street businesses say ferry
OL,4,Aclosure hit trade
OL,5,
OL,6,FA couple who own an Indian restaurant
OL,7,Fon Gravesend's heritage high street
OL,8,Fhave said businesses are struggling
OL,9,Fafter the loss of the ferry service to
OL,10,FTilbury two years ago.
OL,12,FAlim and Rita Khan put everything into
OL,13,Fcreating their dream business, Chaat N
OL,14,FChai, which serves authentic Indian
OL,15,Fstreet food cooked fresh to order.
OL,17,FThey said the high street once saw a
OL,18,Fsteady flow of commuters,
OL,19,Fschoolchildren and day trippers heading
OL,20,Fto and from the ferry, but passing
OL,21,Ftrade has disappeared.
OL,23,APub: 27-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,323,320,200,140,0,100
